==Russian==
{{wp|ru:}}
[[Image:Brosen maja hooks.jpg|thumb|крюк]]

===Etymology===
According to Pokorny, from {{der|ru|ine-pro|*gers-|t=to twist, bend, turn}}, see also {{cog|osx|kerian}}, {{cog|non|keyra|t=to whip}}, also {{cog|grc|γέρδιος|t=weaver}}.<ref>{{R:ine:IEW|392-93}}</ref>

According to Vasmer, the word is borrowed from {{der|ru|non|krókr}}, itself probably from the same Indo-European root.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ru-IPA}}
* {{audio|ru|Ru-крюк.ogg}}
* {{audio|ru|LL-Q7737 (rus)-Tatiana Kerbush-крюк.wav|a=Saint Petersburg}}

===Noun===
{{ru-noun+|b|or|d||-ья|крю́ч|dim=крючо́к}}

# [[hook]]
#: {{ux|ru|[[ру́ки-крю́ки]] ([[у]] [[кто-либо|кого́-либо]])|(someone's) fingers are all thumbs}}
#* {{quote-book|ru|year=1930|author=w:ru:Нина Берберова<t:{{w|Nina Berberova}}>|title=Последние и первые|chapter=III|location=Paris|publisher=Jacques Povolozky & Cie|newversion=English translation from|translator2=w:Marian Schwartz|title2=The Last and the First|location2=London|publisher2=w:Pushkin Press|year2=2021|page2=|pageurl2=
|text=Илья́ прошёл ми́мо пусты́х ка́док и ста́рого верстака́, над кото́рым висе́ла те́рпко па́хнущая ко́нская сбру́я — ли́шняя, ни ра́зу за всё э́то вре́мя не сня́тая с '''крюка́'''.|t=Ilya walked past the empty vats and the old workbench under the acrid-smelling horse harness that hung there—an extra not once taken off its '''hook''' in all this time.}}
# [[detour]]

